### Technical Discussion – NFS Issue & OCP Upgrade

1\. Issue Confirmation: The issue is not yet confirmed as resolved after deploying the suggested workaround.

2\. Version Validation: Check whether the same issue is occurring on other nodes running the same OCP version. Identify the affected nodes and compare their configurations.

3\. OCP Upgrade Limitation: We cannot upgrade the OCP cluster to the suggested version at this time, as OCP 4.22 is already available in the update plan. Request Red Hat to provide a patch or driver fix for the current version.

4\. Temporary Workaround: Request Red Hat's confirmation on whether restarting the affected nodes individually is an acceptable temporary workaround.

5\. Issue Timeline: Confirm when the last OCP upgrade was performed on the affected node. The NFS issue started after the upgrade. Identify the time elapsed between the upgrade and the issue occurrence.

6\. Red Hat Support: Submit the findings to Red Hat Support, tag the concerned team, and request a permanent fix.

### Suggested Message to Red Hat Support

Hi Team,

We are experiencing an NFS-related issue following the recent OCP upgrade.

As OCP 4.22 is already available in the update plan, upgrading to another version is currently not feasible.

We request your assistance with the following:

- Confirm whether the same issue is observed on other nodes running the same OCP version.
- Provide a patch or driver fix for the current OCP version.
- Confirm whether restarting the affected nodes one by one is an acceptable temporary workaround.
- Investigate the issue timeline and its correlation with the recent OCP upgrade.

Please review the issue and provide your recommendations for a permanent resolution.

We will update the support case with the relevant logs and findings.

Thanks.

